 ## Update Log
 
+### 2026-10-27
+- **Board, Priorities and Dump now follow the Projects page's structure; only Plan is left, for Phase 2's Plan week** (component-structure spike, Q1–Q8). Each route reads its data and renders one client container — `BoardPage`, `PrioritiesPage`, `DumpPage` — which owns the page's state, every write and its header, and hands the writes down through a page context; the screen layer (`BoardScreen`, `PrioritiesScreen`, `DumpScreen`) is gone. No behavior changes.
+- **Priorities loses its prop chains**: track, Done, the Move-to popover, the mobile sheet and Add come from `PrioritiesPageContext`, so a quadrant cell and a card take 2 props instead of 9. Grouping by quadrant and "is this card on this week" are pure helpers with unit tests, and the route's week fallback is the adapter `toPrioritiesPageProps`, which the console scenarios run too.
+- **Board and Dump are thin**: the mobile backlog card pulls through `BoardPageContext`; Dump's composer and feed reach capture and load-more through `DumpPageContext`, and the route's feed unwrapping and header week are the adapter `toDumpPageProps`.
